{"content":"# Fixed — hunk-content lines can no longer join the diff path set

`parseDiffPaths` (`js/common/ciViolations.js`) now tracks header-zone state per your suggestion:

- a `diff --git ` line opens the header zone;
- the first `@@` hunk header of each file closes it;
- `--- ` / `+++ ` target lines (and `rename from/to`) only contribute paths **inside the header zone**.

So an added line whose text starts with `++ ` (rendering as `+++ <text>`) or a deleted line starting with `-- ` (rendering as `--- <text>`) after a hunk header is no longer ingested as a phantom path — including the case you flagged where this PR's own diff embeds `diff_pr_433.txt` content. The zone starts open, so a bare `--- a/x` / `+++ b/x` pair without `diff --git` still parses as before.

**Tests added** (`test_ciViolations.js`, suite `hunk content never joins the diff path set`):

- a two-file diff carrying `+++ example of embedded diff text` and `--- not a path` as hunk CONTENT lines → exactly the two real paths, no phantoms (RED before the fix);
- bare `---`/`+++` pair without a `diff --git` header still parses;
- the pinned `#433` fixture (`diff_pr_433.txt`) still yields both real paths — the gating changes nothing for well-formed diffs.

All 55 `test_ciViolations.js` tests pass.
