{"content":"# Fixed — the dismissal scan is scoped; describing a foreign red no longer rejects

`validateOwnedViolationsSummary` / `findDismissalClaim` (`js/common/ciViolations.js`) no longer treat every occurrence of a dismissal phrase as a rejection. The scan now walks the summary line by line and **skips two scopes**:

- **`fixed` / `disputed:` accounting lines** — the structured per-item alternative the gate itself asks for;
- **lines under a foreign-reds section heading** (`/^#{1,6}\s+.*(foreign|infra|do not chase|not chase)/i`, reset by an owned heading like `## Owned CI violations` / `Violations you must fix`) — the foreign note tells the leg to *mention* foreign reds, and "unrelated" is that vocabulary. Your exact repro summary now returns `{ ok: true }`.

The pinned UT-8 intent is preserved: a bare claim in owned/default scope still rejects while owned items are open — including your noted blanket-claim-plus-dispute case (`Not caused by this PR.` on a claim-only line is still found; only the section-structured foreign mention is exempt).

**Tests added** (`js/unit-tests/test_ciViolations.js`, suite `dismissal scan scoping`):

- `a fully-accounted summary that describes a FOREIGN red as "unrelated" passes` → `ok: true` (RED before the change, exactly your repro summary);
- `a dismissal claim OUTSIDE foreign sections still rejects even when a fixed line exists` (conservative direction kept);
- direct `findDismissalClaim` cases: accounting line → null, foreign section → null, bare claim → found, owned-scope claim → found.

All 55 `test_ciViolations.js` tests pass; the two existing UT-8 rejection tests and the blanket-claim-vs-dispute test stayed green unchanged (TDD: written before the fix, RED→GREEN verified).
